title open problem 7: one conflict, a whole generated tree held back

# Section 15, open problem 7.  Quarantine's fixed point is sound but
# not proven minimal, and this is what "not minimal" costs in
# practice.
#
# Off-of razed site/build.  Onto, meanwhile, filled it: a new gen/
# directory with two generated sources, a nested/ directory under
# that, and a table inside that.  Exactly ONE thing is actually in
# dispute -- gen/ survives while the floor it stands on, site/build,
# does not -- and that single structural conflict pulls the entire
# generated subtree into quarantine behind it.  Every one of
# parser.c, parser.h, nested/ and table.inc decided cleanly and on
# its own evidence; each is held back only because its parent's
# parent is disputed, and Definition 12.4 closes over parents.
#
# The count is the point.  Open the inspector and read the quarantine
# list: one conflict, and a queue of components behind it that no
# side disagreed about.  A cleverer analysis might save the ones
# whose whole subtree is unilateral -- but it has to stay sound, and
# nobody has shown a minimal sound quarantine exists or is cheap to
# compute.  Until then over-quarantine is the safe direction, and the
# consolation is that every dragged-in component names the component
# that dragged it, so the report can always answer "why is this
# here?".
#
# site/src is the control: same document, no dispute anywhere near
# it, decides and is emitted.

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: site/
      10-100: build/
        11-100: old.o = old-v1
      12-100: src/
        13-100: main.c = main-v1
        14-100: util.c = util-v1

tree onto
  1-1: /
    2-100: site/
      10-100: build/
        11-100: old.o = old-v1
        # everything below here decides cleanly and none of it is
        # emitted.
        210-200: gen/
          211-200: parser.c = parser-v1
          212-200: parser.h = parserh-v1
          213-200: nested/
            214-200: table.inc = table-v1
      12-100: src/
        13-100: main.c = main-v1
        14-100: util.c = util-v1

tree offof
  1-1: /
    2-100: site/
      # build/ and everything in it is gone.
      12-100: src/
        13-100: main.c = main-v1
        # an ordinary unilateral edit, far from the argument.
        14-100: util.c = util-v2

# --- expected result, generated by gen-expected.js ---
expect conflict structural
expect quarantined /site/build

tree expected
  1-1: /
    2-100: site
      10-100: build
        210-200: gen
          213-200: nested
            214-200: table.inc = table-v1
          211-200: parser.c = parser-v1
          212-200: parser.h = parserh-v1
      12-100: src
        13-100: main.c = main-v1
        14-100: util.c = util-v2
